---
description: Display all UI numbers in Arabic-Indic numerals
globs: client/src/**/*.{tsx,ts}
alwaysApply: true
---

# Arabic-Indic Numerals in the UI

Every number shown to the user on ANY page/component MUST render in Arabic-Indic
numerals (٠١٢٣٤٥٦٧٨٩), never Western digits (0123456789). Applies to serials,
counts, dates, IDs, table cells, page numbers, badges, percentages, etc.

Convert digits at render time with a shared helper:

```typescript
export const toArabicDigits = (val: string | number) =>
  String(val ?? '').replace(/[0-9]/g, d => '٠١٢٣٤٥٦٧٨٩'[Number(d)]);
```

```tsx
// BAD - Western digits shown to the user
<td>{officer.serial}</td>
<span>العدد: {items.length}</span>

// GOOD - Arabic-Indic digits
<td>{toArabicDigits(officer.serial)}</td>
<span>العدد: {toArabicDigits(items.length)}</span>
```

## Dates (order matters, not just digits)

Never pass a raw ISO date (`YYYY-MM-DD`) through `toArabicDigits`. Arabic-Indic
digits are Unicode bidi class AN, so hyphen-separated segments flow right-to-left
and the segments render REVERSED (year ends on the right, day on the left).

Always format read-only dates with the shared `formatDate` helper, which outputs
day-month-year so the day lands on the right in the RTL layout:

```tsx
// BAD - reversed segments (day appears on the left)
<p>بداية اللجنة: {toArabicDigits(committee.lagna_date)}</p>

// GOOD - day-month-year, day on the right
<p>بداية اللجنة: {formatDate(committee.lagna_date)}</p>
```

Inputs and date pickers must show Arabic-Indic digits too:
- Date fields: use the `client/src/components/ArabicDate.tsx` component (NOT a raw
  `<input type="date">`). It shows the value in Arabic-Indic in the field and still
  opens the native picker; `value`/`onChange` stay ISO (`YYYY-MM-DD`). The page also
  sets `lang="ar-EG-u-nu-arab"` which helps the native popup where supported.
- Editable numeric text inputs: display `value={toArabicDigits(state)}` and parse
  typed input back with `toWesternDigits` in `onChange` before storing/sending.

```tsx
<input value={toArabicDigits(form.history_limit)}
  onChange={e => setForm({ ...form,
    history_limit: Number(toWesternDigits(e.target.value).replace(/[^0-9]/g, '')) })} />
```

Rules:
- Underlying STATE, `key`s, `<select>`/`<option value>`, and API payloads stay
  Western. Only the visible digits are Arabic-Indic (convert on the way in/out).
- Use the shared helpers in `client/src/utils/format.ts` (`toArabicDigits`,
  `toWesternDigits`); do not re-declare them per file.
